<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:32:default:default">
<!--
    kuna option mipsunaligned (default on), GH-904: a MIPS unaligned word
    load or store pair lifts as the one whole access it makes.

    MIPS reads an unaligned word with two instructions (lwl $3,1($16);
    lwr $3,4($16) on a big-endian target).  Lifted one at a time each half
    merges memory into the register by a shift its address's low bits
    pick, so the pair read the register it overwrites and printed as a
    tangle of shifts and masks around that value.  After a call that value
    is the call's dead second return word, which made c_unal read add_hi's
    result as a 64-bit pair (and made SQLite's callers of
    sqlite3PagerWrite read it as one, so it printed void):
        v4 = add_hi();
        return ((*(int4 *)((v3 + 1U) - v1) << v1 * 8 | (uint4)((uint8)v4 >> 0x20) & ...   (bug)
    The processor spec's PAIR_INSTRUCTION_FLAG forms make one half do the
    whole access and the other nothing; the flag is now set on both halves
    of every pair before the first decode, as Ghidra's MipsPreAnalyzer
    does.

    Stage: P2 lift and flow (decode-context), option mipsunaligned.  Each
    image is decompiled with the default, then with option mipsunaligned
    off.

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoin_mipsunal
    (bejoin_mipsunal.S; see bejoin_mipspic.provenance) and mipsunaligned_eb.o
    and mipsunaligned_el.o (mipsunaligned.c; see mipsunaligned.provenance).

    Assert #1: c_unal adds the unaligned word to add_hi's int; off, it reads
      add_hi's dead high half.
    Assert #2: get_word returns the word it loads on both byte orders; off,
      it reads the uninitialized result register.
    Assert #3: copy_word copies the word on both byte orders.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">03e0000800000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoin_mipsunal</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu c_unal</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option mipsunaligned off</com>
  <com>lo fu c_unal</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/mipsunaligned_eb.o</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu get_word</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu copy_word</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option mipsunaligned off</com>
  <com>lo fu get_word</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/mipsunaligned_el.o</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu get_word</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu copy_word</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option mipsunaligned off</com>
  <com>lo fu get_word</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="mipsunaligned #1: c_unal adds the unaligned word to add_hi's int" min="1" max="1">return \*\(int4 \*\)\(\(int4\)v1 \+ 1\) \+ v2;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsunaligned #1b: off, c_unal reads add_hi's dead high half" min="1" max="1">\(uint4\)\(\(uint8\)v4 &gt;&gt; 0x20\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsunaligned #2: get_word returns the word it loads on both byte orders" min="2" max="2">return \*\(unsigned int \*\)\(\(int4\)a0 \+ 1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsunaligned #2b: off, get_word reads the uninitialized result register" min="2" max="2">uint4 v3; // v0</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsunaligned #3: copy_word copies the word on both byte orders" min="2" max="2">\*\(unsigned int \*\)\(\(int4\)a0 \+ 1\) = \*\(unsigned int \*\)\(\(int4\)a1 \+ 1\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
